    a: "Usually five to ten years: long enough for the company to reach a steady state, where growth, margins and reinvestment have settled at levels it can sustain. A mature business may need five; a fast grower, a turnaround or a cyclical often needs ten or more. The final year must be normal, because the terminal value capitalizes it.",
