    a: "A company that outgrew the economy forever would eventually become bigger than the economy, so terminal growth is usually set near long-run inflation or nominal GDP growth, often around 2–3%. It must also stay below WACC: as growth approaches WACC, the Gordon formula's denominator shrinks toward zero and value explodes; at or above WACC the formula is meaningless.",
