    why: "The valuation date, the balance sheet and the cash flows must line up. Net debt comes from the latest balance sheet, so cash generated in the first nine months is already in it; counting the full year's cash flow would count those nine months twice. Every discount period is then measured from the valuation date, not from the fiscal year-end. Live deals rarely value a company on its year-end, which is why modeling tests use stubs to check that you know what the discount periods mean.",
